 "soundNote": {
  "kn": "A doubled vowel is held about twice as long. Hold aa, ee, oo like a long note; a, i, u are short notes. Stretching the last vowel to aa also turns any sentence into a question.",
  "hi": "A doubled vowel is held longer: kal versus kaal. Hindi also has a soft breath after some consonants (bh, dh, kh): bhaai, not baai.",
  "ta": "A doubled vowel is held longer: pal versus paal. zh (as in Tamizh, vaazhai) is a soft rolled sound between l and r; most learners start with l and are understood."
 }
